# startRandomPrerecording(Player player)
# Picks a random prerecording slot (0..9) and dispatches playPrerecording
# for it via /function execute — non-blocking, so the caller continues
# running while the mannequin wanders.
#
# Assumes every slot 0..9 has a non-empty recording. Caller is
# responsible for populating them before invoking this.
#
# Auto-spawn: cruiseTo's auto-spawn pattern. If the mannequin hasn't
# been summoned yet, do it now so the /tp targets in playPrerecording
# have something to hit.

@using mannequin
@fast

@if !isSpawned[player]
    @var mannequin::spawnMannequin(player)
@fi

@define Int idx = Int(math::random(0D, 10D))
@if idx >= 10
    @var idx = 9
@fi
@if idx < 0
    @var idx = 0
@fi

# /function execute path is the standard async dispatch (see
# endmap/theCubeAnimation.msc:54 for the same pattern). Use @console
# rather than @bypass — @console queues the command through the
# console-execute path, which is what releases this caller while the
# dispatched MSC function continues to tick on its own @delay loop.
# playPrerecording's @delay 1 yields each tick, so it runs in parallel
# with whatever the caller does next.
@console /function execute mannequin::playPrerecording(Player("{{player.getName()}}"), {{idx}})
